# Runtime-verification evidence must be published *with* the audit package.
#
# The repository-level .gitignore excludes generic `logs`, `*.log`, `artifacts/`
# and `test-results/` paths (correct for application build output). Those rules
# would silently drop every log and JSON capture this audit pass produced, which
# is the opposite of what an evidence package needs. The negations below are
# scoped to developer-review/Evidence/ only — they re-include nothing outside it.
!logs/
!logs/**
!artifacts/
!artifacts/**
!*.log
